# Analyze > CFD table > Solve stability (3D), from a document that already carries its drag table. The headless driver runs every
# task to its end before the next step, so the 3D solve (up to 8 Mach numbers at 2 and 6 degrees) is finished when the screenshot
# is taken: minutes on a fast GPU, far longer on the CPU.
#
# Make the document once:
#   BOWSHOCK_CFD_FIXTURE=/tmp/example-cfd.bowshock cargo test -p bowshock -- --ignored the_example_table --nocapture
# Then:
#   BOWSHOCK_OPEN=/tmp/example-cfd.bowshock cargo run --release -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/cfd-lift.drive out/cfd-lift
viewport 1300x800
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
click "Solve stability (3D)"
click "Aerodynamics"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot lift-dark.png

# Margin, CP and CNα against Mach and against angle of attack.
click "Stability"
move (700, 300)
move (702, 302)
screenshot lift-stability-dark.png
